      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(repair): bind automerge execution to planned head",
        "body": "## Root cause\n\nAutomerge planning produced a deterministic result without recording the exact pull-request head it reviewed. Execution then read the live head and could continue against a newer contributor revision, crossing the planning/execution trust boundary.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Persist `reviewed_sha` in deterministic automerge results.\n- Compare it with the live PR head before target clone, Codex, or push.\n- Write a durable blocked report with `expected_head_sha`, `current_head_sha`, and `requeue_required: true` when the head moved.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run build:all`\n- all source/repair/script/dashboard lint gates\n- repair tests and coverage gates passed\n- container E2E `planning-head-drift` advances the contributor head after planning and proves execution stops before target checkout, Codex, or push\n\nStack 2/3. Base: `feature/automerge-target-runtime`.\n",
        "branch": "feature/automerge-production-fixes",
